<title>USA: U.S. steel service center June shipments off 0.9%.</title>
<headline>U.S. steel service center June shipments off 0.9%.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-07-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>The average daily shipping rate for U.S. steel service centers was 114,600 tons in June, 0.9 percent less than last month, according to the Steel Service Center Institute.</p>
<p>For the first six months of the year, the overall shipping rate for all products is 7.4 percent ahead of last year's corresponding period, led by stainless steel products at 13.2 percent, carbon tubing at 10.8 percent.</p>
<p>((New York Commodity Desk, 212-859-1646))</p>
